title: One hostile turn, end to end — where the revert lands (probe C1, verified)
---
%% Traced from an actual probe run: audit/logs/c1-bash-*.log, 2026-08-18,
%% MINGW64/Windows 11, harness @911878c. The "agent" is a fake binary injected
%% via CODEX_BIN that runs `git commit` mid-turn on purpose — no credentials,
%% no network, no token spend.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant OP as operator / relay-drive
    participant SH as codex-turn.sh<br/>+ relay-turn-lib.sh
    participant AG as fake agent<br/>(CODEX_BIN stub)
    participant TK as tick kernel<br/>(.tick/events)
    participant GIT as git (ROOT)

    OP->>SH: RELAY_AGENT=codex, RELAY_FILE, RELAY_TASK
    SH->>SH: dispatch gate — actor == CODEX_AGENT?
    SH->>TK: tick claim RELAY-TURN --agent codex
    TK-->>SH: won
    SH->>TK: tick info RELAY-TURN
    TK-->>SH: claimer: codex
    Note over SH: ownership PROVEN before the agent<br/>is ever launched (codex-turn.sh:124-129).<br/>Without this, an agent that edits without<br/>the token deadlocks the lane as<br/>apparent "no progress".

    SH->>GIT: rtl_before — snapshot HEAD + dirty set
    GIT-->>SH: HEAD = 1106662, tree clean

    SH->>AG: rtl_run_bounded 30s — launch the agent
    activate AG
    AG->>AG: append a round to relay.md (allowed)
    rect rgb(58, 17, 19)
        AG->>AG: write sneaky.md (off-lane)
        AG->>GIT: git add -A && git commit
        Note right of AG: FORBIDDEN — the agent must never git.<br/>A commit hides its off-lane edits from<br/>`git status`, which is the surface the<br/>allowlist check reads.
        GIT-->>AG: HEAD = 4fd12bb
    end
    AG-->>SH: exit 0 ("success")
    deactivate AG

    Note over SH: the agent reported SUCCESS.<br/>Containment does not trust that.

    SH->>GIT: rtl_enforce — rev-parse HEAD
    GIT-->>SH: 4fd12bb ≠ 1106662 — HEAD MOVED
    SH->>GIT: update-ref refs/relay-orphan/4fd12bb HEAD
    Note right of GIT: the discarded commit stays REACHABLE.<br/>If this was really a concurrent peer<br/>rather than the agent, it is recoverable<br/>via `git log refs/relay-orphan/*`.
    SH->>GIT: git reset --hard 1106662
    GIT-->>SH: tree restored, sneaky.md gone

    SH-->>OP: "codex committed during its turn (forbidden)<br/>— reset to 1106662, failing" → exit 6

    Note over OP,GIT: VERIFIED post-state (audit/logs/c1-bash-4-after.log):<br/>git log = 1106662 only · git status = clean ·<br/>refs/relay-orphan/4fd12bb present · untouchable.md at baseline
